---
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import WorkbenchLab from '../../components/WorkbenchLab.astro';
import { receipt } from '../../labs/workbench/model';
import '../../styles/workbench-lab.css';
---
<BaseLayout title="The portable workbench | David Blumenau" description="Two fictional desks, one real configuration manager. Try a portability decision, then inspect a genuine metacodex drift-refusal and adoption run.">
  <main id="main" class="wb-page">
    <section class="wb-hero wrap" id="top"><a class="wb-return" href="/work/agent-workbench/"><Icon name="arrow-left" /> The agent workbench story</a><div class="wb-hero-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Workbench Lab / A small deliberate mistake</p><h1>Share a setup<br /> <em>and keep local choices.</em></h1></div><div class="wb-hero-copy"><p>I built metacodex to share agent setup between machines while keeping local settings separate. Here, the configuration manager uses two disposable test setups: a conflicting manual edit stops an update until it is deliberately adopted.</p></div></div><div class="wb-hero-foot"><a href="#wb-stage-title">Follow the setup update <Icon name="arrow-down" /></a><span>Actual manager execution · 14 October 2026</span></div></section>
    <div class="wrap"><WorkbenchLab /></div>
    <section class="wb-evidence wrap" aria-labelledby="wb-evidence-title"><div><p class="eyebrow">Executed, then exhibited</p><h2 id="wb-evidence-title">The proof is<br /><em>in the refusal.</em></h2><p>This is a real run of the metacodex configuration manager from a committed source revision. A controlled fixture supplies harmless settings and two disposable homes.</p><p>The interactive desks above illustrate those observed results. The film below records a browser terminal viewer replaying the captured output; its display pacing is editorial.</p></div><div class="wb-proof-cards"><article><span>01 / Exit 1</span><h3>A manual edit survived refusal.</h3><p>Applying over an unadopted reasoning change returned an error. Both the live config and generated snapshot retained their exact hashes.</p></article><article><span>02 / Exit 0</span><h3>Adoption made a local preference durable.</h3><p>Desk A’s high setting moved into its machine overlay and survived the next portable base update. Desk B received the new low default.</p></article><article><span>03 / Six matching hashes</span><h3>Private state stayed at each desk.</h3><p>Two fake auth files, two fake sessions and two fake secret overlays remained byte-for-byte unchanged. The shared skill hash matched on both desks.</p></article></div></section>
    <section class="wb-film wrap" aria-label="Recorded terminal replay"><figure class="video-demo"><div class="video-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Recorded replay / actual CLI output</p><h3>The run, in its own words</h3></div><video controls preload="none" poster="/media/workbench/terminal-replay.webp" playsinline aria-label="The run, in its own words" aria-describedby="wb-film-caption"><source src="/media/workbench/terminal-replay.mp4" type="video/mp4" /><track kind="captions" src="/media/workbench/terminal-replay.vtt" srclang="en" label="English" default />Your browser does not support video playback. <a href="/media/workbench/terminal-replay.mp4">Download the recording.</a></video><figcaption id="wb-film-caption"><strong class="video-provenance">A browser terminal viewer replaying actual captured output. Display pacing is editorial.</strong>Eight real manager commands: installation, drift refusal, explicit adoption, a portable base update and doctor checks. Fixture paths are replaced with $FIXTURE. Observed command durations appear in the replay and receipt.</figcaption><details class="transcript-details"><summary>Read the complete captured output</summary><p>The recording displays one command at a time, followed by the verified configuration and hash results. The deliberate drift refusal is a successful boundary check, with exit 1. All other manager invocations return exit 0.</p><a href="/media/workbench/transcript.txt">Open the full text transcript <Icon name="arrow-up-right" /></a></details></figure></section>
    <section class="wb-receipt wrap" aria-labelledby="wb-receipt-title"><div class="wb-receipt-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Execution receipt</p><h2 id="wb-receipt-title">A claim you can inspect.</h2></div><a href="/media/workbench/receipt.json" class="text-link">Full machine-readable receipt <span aria-hidden="true"><Icon name="arrow-up-right" /></span></a></div>
      <dl class="wb-receipt-facts"><div><dt>Source revision</dt><dd><code>{receipt.revision}</code></dd></div><div><dt>Observed run</dt><dd><time datetime={receipt.testedAt}>{receipt.testedAt.replace('T', ' ').slice(0,19)} UTC</time></dd></div><div><dt>Actual manager commands</dt><dd>8 invocations · 7 successful · 1 deliberate refusal</dd></div><div><dt>Manager SHA-256</dt><dd><code>{receipt.managerSha256}</code></dd></div></dl>
      <details class="wb-receipt-detail"><summary>What the fixture substitutes</summary><ul>{receipt.harness.map(item => <li>{item}</li>)}</ul><p>The fixture uses the archived commit and two disposable homes.</p></details>
      <details class="wb-receipt-detail"><summary>Inspect the protected-file hashes</summary><div class="wb-hash-list">{Object.entries(receipt.desks).map(([name, desk]) => <article><h3>{name === 'desk-a' ? 'Studio desk / A' : 'Travel desk / B'}</h3>{desk.protectedFiles.map(file => <div><strong>{file.path}</strong><span>Before and after match</span><code>{file.sha256Before}</code></div>)}</article>)}</div></details>
      <details class="wb-receipt-detail"><summary>Every command, exit code and observed duration</summary><ol class="wb-invocations">{receipt.steps.map(step => <li><span>{step.desk}</span><code>{step.command}</code><span>exit {step.exitCode} / {step.durationMs} ms</span></li>)}</ol><a href="/media/workbench/transcript.txt" class="text-link">Complete captured transcript <span aria-hidden="true"><Icon name="arrow-up-right" /></span></a></details>
      <details class="wb-receipt-detail"><summary>What this run establishes</summary><ul>{receipt.limitations.map(item => <li>{item}</li>)}</ul><p>The shared skill is linked and readable; this run does not execute its workflow. The doctor result applies to this fixture, including its empty hook configuration.</p></details>
    </section>
    <aside class="wb-context wrap"><p class="eyebrow">The wider workbench</p><p>metaclaude gives portable Claude instructions, hooks and skills a versioned home. metacodex brings the same working idea to Codex with generated configuration, local overlays and explicit drift adoption. This execution tests metacodex’s manager; the <a href="/features/metaclaude/">metaclaude feature story</a> documents the companion project.</p><a href="/features/metacodex/" class="text-link">Follow the source-backed story <span aria-hidden="true"><Icon name="arrow-up-right" /></span></a></aside>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
